# What wlshare-enc-agent.service starts the encoding agent with. Set both, then
#
#   systemctl enable --now wlshare-enc-agent
#
# docs/enc-agent.md, in /usr/share/doc/wlshare-enc-agent, has the rest.

# Where the agent listens: an address of this machine and a port of your
# choosing, which the daemon's [enc_agent] table names.
#LISTEN=192.168.1.20:5990

# Where the wlshare daemon connects from, as IPv4 or IPv6 CIDR blocks with
# commas between them. One address is a /32, or a /128 for IPv6. Name the
# daemon's own address and not its network: every address allowed may try the
# key.
#ALLOW=192.168.1.10/32

# Memory shared with the daemon's virtual machine, where the agent is on its
# host or in a container there: the file the guest's ivshmem-plain device is
# backed by, which the daemon's pictures are written into rather than sent.
# The agent's account has to read and write it; docs/enc-agent.md, "Shared
# memory with the guest", says how. Unset, the pictures cross the network.
#SHARED_MEMORY=/run/ivshmem-wlshare/wlshare
